Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3402787Z ^[[36;1m# failure. Both matter, and for the same reason.^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3403143Z ^[[36;1m#^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3403499Z ^[[36;1m# A pipeline reports its LAST command's status, and cut exits 0 on empty^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3404077Z ^[[36;1m# input -- so `h=$(sha256sum ... | cut) || h=unhashed` can never take its^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3404640Z ^[[36;1m# fallback. A missing hasher would leave h empty and the key would read^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3405194Z ^[[36;1m# "Linux-datasets-": the constant this step exists to eliminate,^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3405756Z ^[[36;1m# reintroduced silently. Python also removes the portability question,^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3406345Z ^[[36;1m# since setup-python above guarantees it and sha256sum is coreutils-only.^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:17:23.3406812Z ^[[36;1m#^[[0m
