Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5121165Z ^[[36;1m# failure. Both matter, and for the same reason.^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5121486Z ^[[36;1m#^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5121825Z ^[[36;1m# A pipeline reports its LAST command's status, and cut exits 0 on empty^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5122340Z ^[[36;1m# input -- so `h=$(sha256sum ... | cut) || h=unhashed` can never take its^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5122853Z ^[[36;1m# fallback. A missing hasher would leave h empty and the key would read^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5123358Z ^[[36;1m# "Linux-datasets-": the constant this step exists to eliminate,^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5123866Z ^[[36;1m# reintroduced silently. Python also removes the portability question,^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5124565Z ^[[36;1m# since setup-python above guarantees it and sha256sum is coreutils-only.^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5124966Z ^[[36;1m#^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5125274Z ^[[36;1m# No `|| default` here at all: a key that cannot be computed must fail^[[0m
Benchmark amd64 (abr)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-15T00:36:54.5125774Z ^[[36;1m# the run loudly. Degrading to any fixed string rebuilds the same^[[0m
